    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "994a046a8f706d11d438bb91fbd7264e5454f92373aaa83e0736825b036f6a86",
      "text": "Breakfast and tourist bus to Puno, with a stop at Andahuaylillas and its Church of San Pedro, the “Sistine Chapel of South America”, built on the foundations of an Inca temple, modest outside and richly painted within; then Raqchi, at 3,500 metres, with the 92-by-25-metre Temple of Wiracocha, notable for the 22 columns that once supported its roof. Buffet lunch in Sicuani, stops at the La Raya pass, at more than 4,300 metres, and at Pucará and its Lithic Museum. Arrival around 18:00 in Puno, capital of the Puno region, at about 3,830 metres on the shores of Lake Titicaca.\n\nOptional: PeruRail Titicaca train, Cusco – Puno · Day 6 (+ $ 250 per person; Wednesdays, Fridays and Sundays). Instead of the bus: dining, bar and observation cars on one of the world’s highest railways, a stop at La Raya (4,319 m) and a three-course lunch. Arrival in Puno around 19:00.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_aligned",
